# Milestone: M5
# Covers: multiple subscribers on the same event receive emits in registration
#         FIFO order; D-event-1 rule (spec #3 §10.2); 3 subs on 3 emits.
#
# blocked: subscriber walk order not observable from script — log-building pattern needs slot-write ordering verified across spawn (audit Cat. E)
# matrix-row: reactive-event
#
# Reason:
#   Same blockers as event_emit_async.chk.  The FIFO walk of event->at_watchers_head
#   is exercised by test_uevent_subscribe.c and test_event_emit_async.c at the
#   C-level unit tests.  The scripted fixture requires Event.new() T59 binding
#   and scratch-frame body dispatch.
#
# Activate when Event.new() + scratch-frame body dispatch are wired.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at T59 + M5-scratch-frame):
#   var e = Event.new();
#   var seq = "";
#   at (e?) Realm.seq = Realm.seq + "A";
#   at (e?) Realm.seq = Realm.seq + "B";
#   at (e?) Realm.seq = Realm.seq + "C";
#   e!; e!;
#   seq
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000000] nil
#   [00000001] ""
#   [00000002] nil
#   [00000003] nil
#   [00000004] nil
#   [00000005] nil
#   [00000006] nil
#   [00000007] "ABCABC"
